---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-html-editor</code> is a form field for rich text whose value has to
  be HTML, such as an email body or a CMS field. It is the same editor as
  <code>wc-markdown-editor</code>: people edit formatted text directly, the way
  they would in a word processor, and the value is HTML.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Toolbar</strong>: text style, bold, italic, underline,
    strikethrough, inline code, link, lists, checklist, quote, code block,
    table, divider and mention. While the caret is in a table, a
    <em>Table</em> menu adds and removes rows and columns, and column edges
    can be dragged to resize them.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Selection bubble</strong>: select text to format it in place.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Slash menu</strong>: type <code>/</code> to insert a block.
    Markdown shortcuts such as <code>## </code>, <code>- </code>,
    <code>1. </code>, <code>&gt; </code> and <code>**bold**</code> work as you
    type.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Block handle</strong>: hover a block to drag it, or press
    <strong>+</strong> to insert a block below.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Link</strong>: the toolbar button, the bubble or
    <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>/<kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> open the link editor. Only web,
    email and relative addresses are accepted.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>View source</strong>: the last toolbar button shows the HTML,
    which you can edit directly.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  HTML can store underline and table column widths, which Markdown cannot, so
  the HTML editor offers them. Only what the editor supports is kept: other
  tags, attributes and scripts in a value are dropped when it loads.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-html-editor
    id="html-editor"
    label="Message"
    helper-text="Type / for blocks, select text to format, @ to mention."
    style="display:block; width: 100%;"
  ></wc-html-editor>
  <script is:inline src="/assets/js/mention-demo.js"></script>
  <script is:inline>
    // Answers `search` with people (@) and tickets (#), so mentions list suggestions.
    window.peacockMentionDemo(document.getElementById('html-editor'));
    document.getElementById('html-editor').value = `<h2>Billing export update</h2>
<p>Hi team, the <strong>CSV export</strong> fails for last month. Please <u>review the steps</u> before stand-up.</p>
<ol>
  <li><p>Open the <strong>billing</strong> page as an admin</p></li>
  <li><p>Export last month as <em>CSV</em></p></li>
</ol>
<ul data-type="taskList">
  <li data-type="taskItem" data-checked="true"><p>Reproduced on staging</p></li>
  <li data-type="taskItem" data-checked="false"><p>Reproduced on production</p></li>
</ul>
<table>
  <tr><th><p>Region</p></th><th><p>Status</p></th></tr>
  <tr><td><p>EU</p></td><td><p>Failing</p></td></tr>
  <tr><td><p>US</p></td><td><p>OK</p></td></tr>
</table>`;
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3 class="text-title-medium">Without the toolbar</h3>

<p>
  <code>hide-toolbar</code> leaves a clean writing surface. Formatting stays
  available from the selection bubble, the slash menu, Markdown shortcuts and
  keyboard shortcuts.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-html-editor
    label="Notes"
    hide-toolbar
    rows="3"
    placeholder="Write a note. Select text to format it."
    style="display:block; width: 100%;"
  ></wc-html-editor>
</DemoComponentCard>
